          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              The statement of the Quillen adjunctions appears as
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, prop A.3.3.7
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, prop A.3.3.8
          %p
            In fact homotopy Kan extension forms as above forms a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjoint+triple"} Quillen adjoint triple
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "Quillen+adjoint+triple#QuillenAdjointTripleHomotopyKanExtension"} there
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Since, intrinsically, Kan extensions, as every
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+construction"} universal construction
            %p
              Given
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \in [C,A]
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \in [C',A]
              and a morphism
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi η
                      %mo :
                      %mi G
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta : G \to f_* F
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
              %strong
                exhibits
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                as a homotopy right Kan extension
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              if for some injectively fibrant replacement
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo →
                    %mover
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \to \hat F
              the composite morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi F
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \to f_* F \to f_* \hat F
              is a weak equivalence.
            %p
              So
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_* \hat F
              here is a homotopy Kan extension as produced by the derived functor, while
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              may be a more general object, weakly equivalent to it.
          %h3#properties Properties
          %h4#HomIntoKanExt Derived-hom into a ho-Kan extension is a ho-Kan extention
          %p
            Recall that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : C \to A
            an ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            between ordinary
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi lim
                    %mo ←
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lim_\leftarrow F
            is characterized by the fact that for every object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
            the set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
